    "type": "01 73",
    "kind": "graph",
    "made_by": "backup/build-lo-fi-models.py"
  },
  "sample_rate_hz": 32000,
  "why_this_rate": "The clock this unit's other types are read at; the noise claim reads its one-pole corners at it. Nothing on this type drawn here names a rate.",
  "inputs": [
    "in_l",
    "in_r"
  ],
  "outputs": {
    "out_l": "high_l",
    "out_r": "high_r"
  },
  "what_varies": "The type's filter is one bilinear pole, as the identically printed pre filter of the stereo chorus was read. In Stereo the pan byte does nothing; it places only the mono sum.",
  "what_is_not_modelled": [
    "All four generators -- radio noise, white or pink noise, disc noise and hum -- and every byte that sets them. The radio noise powers up at 64, so if it sounds with its detune at 0, every take at power-on carries noise no candidate draws.",
    "The Lo-Fi Type byte, which no record reads.",
    "The level of the path through the type against the path past it: no record on this type reads it, so the path is drawn at unity before the balance."
  ],
  "fixed_rows": {
    "40 03 03": "Lo-Fi Type: no record reads this byte and no claim or document gives it a quantity; the degrader closed on the other Lo-Fi type is a different byte over a different range and is not carried here.",
    "40 03 06": "R.Detune: what it does is read nowhere.",
    "40 03 07": "R.Nz Lev: a noise generator's level, and this renderer has no noise source.",
    "40 03 08": "W/P Sel: picks a noise generator's colour; no noise source is drawn.",
    "40 03 09": "W/P LPF: the noise claim reads it as a one-pole corner table, but it filters only a generator that is not drawn.",
    "40 03 0A": "W/P Level: a noise generator's level; no noise source is drawn.",
    "40 03 0B": "Disc Type: a noise generator's character; no noise source is drawn.",
    "40 03 0C": "Disc LPF: the noise claim reads it on the same table as W/P LPF, but it filters only a generator that is not drawn.",
    "40 03 0D": "Disc Nz Lev: a noise generator's level; no noise source is drawn.",
    "40 03 0E": "Hum Type: a hum generator's mains frequency; no hum is drawn.",
    "40 03 0F": "Hum LPF: filters only the hum, which is not drawn.",
    "40 03 10": "Hum Level: the hum's level; no hum is drawn."
  },
